  "brief_rationale": "The doctor recognized severe progressive radial nerve dysfunction and repeatedly moved the family from online uncertainty to same-system hand-surgery/peripheral-nerve follow-up, then to a documented admission-registration pathway. Diabetes privacy was handled safely: the doctor insisted the surgical/anesthesia team must know while giving concrete confidentiality language and medication-safety boundaries. Closure was traceable and executable after the family obtained a registration number, callback phone, time window, medication plan, and red-flag escalation threshold. Multiple high-order actions were completed, including privacy-sensitive communication, eliciting/using diabetes and medication information, executable scripts/checklists, and repairing mistaken assumptions about “already scheduled” care.",
